<header class="hero" id="top">
  <img class="cover-amb" src="/assets/img/hero-amb.jpg" alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="96" height="120">
  <div class="hero-inner">
    <h1 class="masthead cond" id="masthead"><span class="mline"><span class="mw">Reggie</span> <span class="mw">James</span></span></h1>
    <div class="cover-stack">
      <img class="cover-bg" src="/assets/img/hero.webp" fetchpriority="high" width="1122" height="1402" alt="" aria-hidden="true">
      <img class="cover-cut" src="/assets/img/hero-cut.webp" width="1122" height="1402" alt="Reggie James in a navy blazer and open-neck shirt, arms folded" fetchpriority="high">
    </div>
    <div class="cover-left">
      <p class="lead">I build technology businesses and take them to market.</p>
      <a class="pill" href="#story">See my career</a>
    </div>
    <div class="cover-right">
      <ul>
        <li><b>Founder and Managing Director</b><span>Digital Clarity</span></li>
        <li><b>COO and Executive Director</b><span>DBMM Group Inc. (OTC: DBMM)</span></li>
        <li><b>25 years</b><span>Search, digital and AI</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <span class="scroll-cue" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  </div>
</header>

<section class="band statement" id="statement" aria-label="Introduction">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p id="statementText">I have worked in technology markets for 25 years, through search, digital and now AI. I founded Digital Clarity in 2002 and built DC Storm within it through to its acquisition by Rakuten. Since 2011 I have also held executive and board roles at DBMM Group, a US public company. Today I work with founders, CEOs and investors on go-to-market, brand and applied AI.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band dark proof" aria-labelledby="proof-h">
  <div class="proof-bg" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/assets/img/office-night.webp" alt="" loading="lazy"></div>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="proof-head">
      <h2 class="h-sec" id="proof-h">Selected results</h2>
      <p>From DC Storm and from client programmes led by Digital Clarity.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="figures">
      <div class="fig"><b>48<small>%</small></b><p><strong>DC Storm adoption</strong>of major media planning and buying agencies used the platform before Rakuten acquired it.</p></div>
      <div class="fig"><b>$23<small>M</small></b><p><strong>ARR, up from $8m</strong>Software client growth supported over three years.</p></div>
      <div class="fig"><b>88<small>%</small></b><p><strong>EMEA revenue growth</strong>in 12 months for an enterprise software client, with cost per acquisition down 37.6%.</p></div>
      <div class="fig"><b>200<small>+</small></b><p><strong>Clients</strong>including Adobe, Xerox and Bentley Systems, across the UK, Europe, the US and Asia.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band" id="story" aria-labelledby="story-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="chap-head">
      <h2 class="h-sec" id="story-h">Career</h2>
      <p>Commercial roles in technology publishing and early internet search, then 20 years building Digital Clarity, a product exit and a US public-company board role.</p>
    </div>
    <ol class="chapters">
      <li class="chapter">
        <span class="n">01</span>
        <h3><span class="when">Earlier career</span>VNU and Ziff Davis</h3>
        <div class="body"><p>Technology publishing and advertising sales roles across Europe. A grounding in technology markets, enterprise customers and commercial growth.</p></div>
              </li>
      <li class="chapter">
        <span class="n">02</span>
        <h3><span class="when">Before 2002</span>AltaVista and Singapore</h3>
        <div class="body"><p>AltaVista's global sales team in the formative years of internet search, working with HP and Compaq. Then a senior commercial role at a Singapore internet business that listed on SIMEX and was acquired by an Indian technology company.</p><span class="tag">Listed, then acquired</span></div>
        <img class="pic" src="/assets/img/trails-vertical.webp" width="900" height="1600" alt="Light trails from traffic passing a lit building at night" loading="lazy">
      </li>
      <li class="chapter">
        <span class="n">03</span>
        <h3><span class="when">2002</span>Digital Clarity</h3>
        <div class="body"><p>Founded the business and built it to 25 to 30 people working with more than 200 clients. Evolved the offer from search and performance marketing into strategic growth and go-to-market advisory.</p><span class="tag">Founder</span></div>
        <img class="pic" src="/assets/img/office-night.webp" width="2000" height="1125" alt="A team working late in a lit office, seen from the street at night" loading="lazy">
      </li>
      <li class="chapter">
        <span class="n">04</span>
        <h3><span class="when">Built within Digital Clarity</span>DC Storm</h3>
        <div class="body"><p>Identified the difficulty of measuring marketing performance across fragmented digital channels and built a technology proposition to address it. Led product, positioning, sales and partnerships through to customer adoption. Around 48% of major media planning and buying agencies used the platform before its acquisition by Rakuten.</p><span class="tag amber">Acquired by Rakuten</span></div>
        <div class="pic-blank" aria-hidden="true"><b>48%</b><span>of major media agencies on the platform at exit</span></div>
      </li>
      <li class="chapter">
        <span class="n">05</span>
        <h3><span class="when">2011</span>DBMM Group</h3>
        <div class="body"><p>COO, Senior Vice President and Executive Director of Digital Brand Media &amp; Marketing Group, Inc., quoted in the US as OTC: DBMM, with Digital Clarity as its wholly owned operating business.</p><span class="tag">US public company</span></div>
        <img class="pic" src="/assets/img/tower.webp" width="1600" height="1066" alt="An office building at night with every floor lit" loading="lazy">
      </li>
      <li class="chapter">
        <span class="n">06</span>
        <h3><span class="when">Today</span>Advisory</h3>
        <div class="body"><p>Working with technology leaders, professional advisers and investors on go-to-market, brand and applied AI, as AI changes how buyers research and buy.</p><span class="tag">Advisory</span></div>
        <img class="pic" src="/assets/img/london-night.webp" width="1800" height="1201" alt="A London bus leaving light trails across a bridge at night" loading="lazy">
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band" id="companies" aria-labelledby="co-h" style="padding-top:0">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 class="h-sec" id="co-h">Digital Clarity and DBMM</h2>
    <div class="two">
      <article class="co dc">
        <p class="role">Founder and Managing Director, since 2002</p>
        <h3>Digital Clarity</h3>
        <p>A growth and go-to-market advisory for technology, software and financial-services businesses. I own the P&amp;L, pricing and team, and work directly with CEOs, founders and senior teams to diagnose barriers to growth and agree where to focus. The work joins three disciplines: commercial go-to-market, brand and applied AI.</p>
        <div class="facts">
          <div><b>2002</b><span>Founded</span></div>
          <div><b>200+</b><span>Clients</span></div>
          <div><b>25&ndash;30</b><span>People</span></div>
        </div>
        <a class="textlink" href="https://www.digital-clarity.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">digital-clarity.com</a>
      </article>
      <article class="co db">
        <span class="ticker"><i aria-hidden="true"></i>OTC: DBMM</span>
        <p class="role">COO, Senior Vice President and Executive Director, since 2011</p>
        <h3>DBMM Group Inc.</h3>
        <p>Digital Clarity is the wholly owned operating business of Digital Brand Media &amp; Marketing Group, Inc., a US public company. I lead the operating business and hold executive and board responsibilities for the group.</p>
        <ul class="duties">
          <li>Group strategy, operating performance, P&amp;L and forecasting</li>
          <li>Board decisions on partnerships, corporate development and investment</li>
          <li>SEC reporting, OTC Markets requirements and governance, with US accountants and lawyers</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band dark" id="capabilities" aria-labelledby="cap-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 class="h-sec" id="cap-h">Areas of experience</h2>
    <div class="caps">
      <div class="cap"><h3>Go-to-market strategy</h3><p>Propositions, positioning and market-entry plans built from customer conversations, market data and workshops, then carried through sales, marketing and product.</p><span class="proofline">$8m to $23m ARR in three years</span></div>
      <div class="cap"><h3>Business development</h3><p>My career started in sales. Global accounts at AltaVista, agency and technology partnerships at DC Storm, enterprise clients at Digital Clarity, in the UK, Europe, the US and Asia.</p><span class="proofline">HP, Compaq, Adobe, Xerox, Bentley Systems</span></div>
      <div class="cap"><h3>Building and exiting</h3><p>Taking a product from market need through development, commercialisation and customer adoption to exit.</p><span class="proofline">DC Storm to Rakuten. Singapore listing and acquisition.</span></div>
      <div class="cap"><h3>Public-company leadership</h3><p>Executive and board work in a US listed company: strategy, forecasting, corporate development, SEC reporting and shareholder governance.</p><span class="proofline">OTC: DBMM since 2011</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band" id="approach" aria-labelledby="ap-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 class="kicker" id="ap-h" style="margin-bottom:28px">How I work</h2>
    <p class="quote">I start with the outcome and the evidence: speak to customers, examine the data and identify what is preventing progress. I stay involved through delivery and take responsibility for the result.</p>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li><span class="sn">01</span><h3>Evidence</h3><p>Customer conversations, market and performance data, and what is holding growth back.</p></li>
      <li><span class="sn">02</span><h3>Diagnosis</h3><p>Agree where to focus, including how AI and changing buyer behaviour affect the route to market.</p></li>
      <li><span class="sn">03</span><h3>Plan</h3><p>Priorities, resource decisions and a plan that teams can execute.</p></li>
      <li><span class="sn">04</span><h3>Delivery</h3><p>Commercial, product and finance working together, and responsibility for the result.</p></li>
    </ol>
    <div class="areas" aria-label="Areas of experience">
      <span>P&amp;L and commercial planning</span><span>Customer and market insight</span><span>Proposition development</span><span>Product commercialisation</span><span>Market entry</span><span>Sales and marketing alignment</span><span>Partnerships</span><span>Public-company governance</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

